 ## Buddy poses available
 
 Only `point` and `sit` exist. The others fall back: peek, walk, thumbs and pop → point; wave and confused → sit.
+
+## Performance policy (LCP-safe motion)
+
+- **Hard load = complete first paint.** Nothing in the first viewport is hidden or animated on a hard load (no loader, no client navigation yet). `globals.css` hides `[data-yb-anim]` only under `html[data-yb-softnav]` (set by `SmoothScroll` on the first client-side pathname change) and only until the effect marks the element ready. Under the home loader (`html[data-yb-loader]`) the page is painted as is underneath the opaque curtain; JS puts the hero in its start pose before the curtain leaves.
+- `data-yb-anim` values: `""` (below the fold: JS decides), `"children"`, `"lcp"` and `"lcp-children"` (first viewport by construction). `data-yb-ready="wait"` = JS is alive and the element waits for the reader (hidden, no failsafe timer).
+- Non-`lcp` elements on a hard load: `revealOnView` (in `motion/entrance.ts`) leaves anything already in the first viewport as painted and hides what is below the fold until it is reached. After a client navigation or under the loader it always holds the element until the reveal line.
+- **Idle setup.** ScrollTriggers (pins, scrubs, drifting shapes) are built through `defer()` / `deferIn(contextSafe, fn)` (`motion/entrance.ts`): after first paint (FCP), one job per idle task, then a single `ScrollTrigger.refresh()` (`scheduleRefresh`). ScrollTrigger is loaded lazily (`loadScrollTrigger()` in `motion/gsap.ts`; `ScrollTrigger` is a live binding, only touch it in deferred work). Lenis is loaded after first paint too.
+- When tweening many elements at once, call `warm(els)` (`motion/gsap.ts`) first: it reads every element's transform in one pass so GSAP does not force a style recalculation per element.
+- Scroll handlers must not read layout per event: measure on refresh/resize (see `PdpFlight`, `OccasionStrip`, `BuddyIntro`).
+- Images: only the LCP image gets `priority` (preload, fetchpriority high); other first-viewport images use `PackImage eager`.
+- The display font is a local, weight-800-pinned subset (`src/app/fonts/`, 74 KB instead of 129 KB).
